What is Metal Heat Treating?
Metal heat treating comprises a range of controlled thermal processes that alter the physical and mechanical properties of metals and alloys. These metallurgical techniques - including annealing, quenching, tempering, case hardening, and normalizing - are essential for improving material characteristics like hardness, strength, ductility, and resistance to wear and corrosion.
